scope='This guide covers pemetrexed on its own for maintenance or second-line treatment of selected non-squamous non-small-cell lung cancer. If pembrolizumab or another immunotherapy is also prescribed, use the matching combination regimen and its additional consent, monitoring and urgent advice. Pemetrexed with pembrolizumab maintenance is a different treatment plan.'
purpose='Pemetrexed is chemotherapy used to control selected non-squamous non-small-cell lung cancer that is locally advanced or has spread. Maintenance aims to keep cancer controlled after platinum chemotherapy has finished without the cancer progressing. Second-line treatment is a separate treatment decision after previous chemotherapy. Ask which aim and indication apply to you.'
duration='Treatment is planned every three weeks while it is helping and side effects remain acceptable. There is no fixed total number of cycles in this regimen. Scans, symptoms, blood results, your priorities and the oncology review guide continuation, delays, changes or stopping.'
administration='Pemetrexed is infused into a vein over about 10 minutes on Day 1. The whole visit is longer because it includes blood-result review, symptom checks, medicines, preparation and observation. The team can use a cannula or suitable existing line; this regimen has no routine take-home infusion pump.'
evidence_summary='Maintenance studies found longer disease control or survival with pemetrexed than placebo in selected patients whose cancer had not progressed after initial chemotherapy. One studied starting pemetrexed after a different chemotherapy combination; another studied continuing it after pemetrexed and cisplatin. A separate second-line study found similar survival to docetaxel with fewer important blood-count side effects. These historical comparisons do not predict an individual outcome or describe pemetrexed plus immunotherapy.'
urgent='Call your oncology 24-hour number immediately for a temperature of 37.5°C or above, 36°C or below, shivering or sudden illness. Call urgently for new breathlessness, chest pain, bleeding, severe or persistent diarrhoea, vomiting despite medicines, inability to drink, very little urine or a spreading or blistering rash. Do not wait for the next visit; serious infection can occur without a high temperature.'
consent='Discuss whether this is maintenance or second-line treatment, the individual aim, likely benefit and uncertainty, alternatives including not proceeding, common and serious harms, possible lasting kidney or nerve effects, fertility and pregnancy, vitamin and steroid medicines, practical burdens and your right to reconsider. A discussion aid supports but does not replace informed consent.'
folate='The source uses folic acid 350–1000 micrograms daily. Take at least five doses in the seven days before the first pemetrexed, continue throughout treatment and for 21 days after the final dose. Follow your own prescription and tell the team about missed doses.'
b12='The source uses vitamin B12 1000 micrograms into a muscle during the week before the first pemetrexed, then every three cycles. Later injections may be on treatment day. A change from platinum treatment to maintenance does not automatically restart the B12 clock: your team checks the last dose and the next due date.'
steroid='Pemetrexed rash prevention uses dexamethasone-equivalent 4 mg twice daily on the day before, day of and day after treatment. Your pharmacist or prescriber should give one clear steroid schedule that also accounts for any anti-sickness medicines. Do not add a second steroid course yourself.'
interactions='Check with the team before using ibuprofen, other anti-inflammatory painkillers, aspirin or any new medicine. Kidney function and the medicine determine whether and when it needs interruption. Do not stop a prescribed medicine on your own; ask for a written plan.'
